<title>USA: Major states-U.S. winter/durum wheat plantings.</title>
<headline>Major states-U.S. winter/durum wheat plantings.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA 1997 winter wheat plantings, spring wheat intentions, major states(1,000 acres).</p>
<p>WINTER WHEAT, Major States (Pct 1997/96):</p>
<p>    -   PCT--IND'97--(PREV)--PLANT'96  PLANT'95</p>
<p> Colo   103   3,100   3,100   3,000     2,900</p>
<p> Kans    97  11,400  11,400  11,800    11,700</p>
<p> Neb     87   2,000   2,000   2,300     2,150</p>
<p> Okla    97   6,800   6,800   7,000     6,900</p>
<p> Texas  100   6,000   6,000   6,000     5,800</p>
<p> Wash    94   2,250   2,250   2,400     2,250</p>
<p> U.S.    93  48,227  48,222  51,983    48,686</p>
<p>DURUM WHEAT, All States:</p>
<p>    -   PCT--IND'97--(PREV)--PLANT'96  PLANT'95</p>
<p> Ariz    61     100     105     165	 100</p>
<p> Cal     93     130     115     140	  70</p>
<p>    -   PCT  IND'97  PLANT'96  PLANT'95</p>
<p> Minn    50	 5	10	  13</p>
<p> Mont   114     320     280	 270</p>
<p> N.D.    87   2,600   3,000     2,950</p>
<p> S.D.   120	30	25	  33</p>
<p> U.S.    88   3,185   3,620     3,436</p>
<p>OTHER SPRING WHEAT, Major States (Indicated 1997, Planted 1996, Pct of 1997/96):</p>
<p>    -   PCT  IND'97  PLANT'96  PLANT'95</p>
<p> Ida     83     600     720	 580</p>
<p> Minn    98   2,500   2,550     2,250</p>
<p> Mont    95   4,000   4,200     3,950</p>
<p> N.D.    80   7,700   9,600     8,300</p>
<p> S.D.    98   2,250   2,300     1,250</p>
<p> Wash   113     450     400	 450</p>
<p> U.S.    89  17,775  20,036    17,010</p>
<p>Previously reported 1997 plantings data for winter wheat and for durum wheat in Arizona and California were issued by USDA in January.</p>
